## Summary

Implemented issue #15: bumped the entire fumadocs + Next.js + React dependency graph together to peer-compatible versions:

- `fumadocs-core`/`fumadocs-ui` → 16.14.5, `fumadocs-mdx` → 15.3.0, `fumadocs-typescript` → 5.3.0, `@fumadocs/cli` → 1.4.1, `next` → 16.3.1, `react`/`react-dom` → 19.2.8
- Also bumped `eslint` (^8→^9) and `eslint-config-next` (^15→^16), which was necessary fallout since eslint-config-next tracks Next's major and v16 only ships flat-config exports requiring eslint ≥9
- Replaced `.eslintrc.json` with `eslint.config.mjs` (flat config composing `eslint-config-next/core-web-vitals` + `.../typescript`, plus an `.source/**` ignore since eslint 9 no longer implicitly skips dot-directories)

During the code-review pass (via `/code-review` against `origin/epic/13-fumadocs-stack-update`), the Standards sub-agent caught a real regression I'd introduced — my initial flat-config migration silently dropped the `next/typescript` ruleset — which I fixed by adding it back explicitly. The Spec sub-agent flagged that migration notes weren't captured anywhere; I addressed that with a detailed commit message covering the fumadocs-mdx v11→v15 (skips v12-14), fumadocs-core/ui v15→v16, and fumadocs-typescript v4→v5 breaking changes, plus a code comment in `source.config.ts` calling out the specific `.source/` output-shape change I discovered (v15 emits `server.ts`/`dynamic.ts`/`browser.ts` instead of `index.ts`) that later tickets will need to handle.

`pnpm install` completes cleanly with no peer conflicts, and the fumadocs-mdx postinstall codegen runs without erroring. As the issue anticipates, `tsc --noEmit` (5 errors) and part of `eslint .` (6 problems) still fail against pre-existing consumer code that hasn't been migrated to the new APIs yet — that's explicitly deferred to tickets 3-5. Work is committed on the `feat/15-fumadocs-dependency-bump` branch.

